    {
      "id": "Uc13LeZhq5IlhYvgay4pq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 885.607243129186,
      "y": 3289.5953456333727,
      "width": 958.7193603515625,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2019103963,
      "version": 1009,
      "versionNonce": 2047223445,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779513934917,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Non-functonal\n1) we did scaling by adding multiple instance of chat server\n2) Availability also resolve by adding instances and db (master slave replica)\n3) SPOF also resolved \n\nProblems\n0) Message deliver is still not gureented as any chat server down then what ?\n1) WebSocket connection mapping\n    solution 1: Store in db ( user -> websocket connection)\n    -> not realistic as for each time need to call db which consume more time and add more latency\n    Solution 2: Store in redis\n    -> which is fast and required less time so reduce latency\n    problem: if user disconnected with WebSocket when you will going to update Redis and how. \n    \n2) If user disconnected with websokcet then how message deliver to user.\n3) when user is online how he will received all pending messages.\n \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Non-functonal\n1) we did scaling by adding multiple instance of chat server\n2) Availability also resolve by adding instances and db (master slave replica)\n3) SPOF also resolved \n\nProblems\n0) Message deliver is still not gureented as any chat server down then what ?\n1) WebSocket connection mapping\n    solution 1: Store in db ( user -> websocket connection)\n    -> not realistic as for each time need to call db which consume more time and add more latency\n    Solution 2: Store in redis\n    -> which is fast and required less time so reduce latency\n    problem: if user disconnected with WebSocket when you will going to update Redis and how. \n    \n2) If user disconnected with websokcet then how message deliver to user.\n3) when user is online how he will received all pending messages.\n \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
