    {
      "id": "YnmDDelaQR_DVihyoX-_D",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 880.607243129186,
      "y": 3777.0953456333727,
      "width": 1141.6392822265625,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4y",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1617186869,
      "version": 2335,
      "versionNonce": 236957563,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779514597733,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Message gureente deliered\n1) message failed before reach chat server: we need retry option to try two or more time with idompotent end point.\n2) chat server failed after save message in db.\nSolutions:\n1) Retrive it and send back to user ( but still not gurentee)\n2) Use kafka to deliver it, based on chat we can create topics so whoever subscrive it will received message.\n -> overhead on kafka ( user1 -> have 200 chat than 20M -> 2000M topics need)\n -> Same if create based on user ( user 1 -> have 3 chat than 20 M -> 60M topics need)\nand again we are storing message as well which become problem.\n3) Use redis pub-sub to send notification to all subscribe users to received message publish in chat.\n-> No overhead, simple raise and forget.\n\n\nWhen user is online How old not received message send back to user.\n1) Store status in db and when ack get message received update status of message in db.\nso when user online retrieve all message and send it back to user.\nhere we will do read call to replica instead of master ( for overhead)\n\n2) Store counter in db and pass counter with message to client.\nso when client get online it will ask server to give me all message after the counter.\n-> again overhead because multiple user try to access they have to put a lock ( db internally do it)\n\n3) Store counter in redis and db . \nuser redis to increment counter and when all done update that counter in db.\n\n\nHow to know user is discounneted\n1) we need to send heatbeat to each websocket to know they are avaiable or not\nSolution\nI) we need to store in db about their active\nii) we need to store in redis aboue their active.\niii) we will use hasing to be sure websocket connection and entries in redis.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Message gureente deliered\n1) message failed before reach chat server: we need retry option to try two or more time with idompotent end point.\n2) chat server failed after save message in db.\nSolutions:\n1) Retrive it and send back to user ( but still not gurentee)\n2) Use kafka to deliver it, based on chat we can create topics so whoever subscrive it will received message.\n -> overhead on kafka ( user1 -> have 200 chat than 20M -> 2000M topics need)\n -> Same if create based on user ( user 1 -> have 3 chat than 20 M -> 60M topics need)\nand again we are storing message as well which become problem.\n3) Use redis pub-sub to send notification to all subscribe users to received message publish in chat.\n-> No overhead, simple raise and forget.\n\n\nWhen user is online How old not received message send back to user.\n1) Store status in db and when ack get message received update status of message in db.\nso when user online retrieve all message and send it back to user.\nhere we will do read call to replica instead of master ( for overhead)\n\n2) Store counter in db and pass counter with message to client.\nso when client get online it will ask server to give me all message after the counter.\n-> again overhead because multiple user try to access they have to put a lock ( db internally do it)\n\n3) Store counter in redis and db . \nuser redis to increment counter and when all done update that counter in db.\n\n\nHow to know user is discounneted\n1) we need to send heatbeat to each websocket to know they are avaiable or not\nSolution\nI) we need to store in db about their active\nii) we need to store in redis aboue their active.\niii) we will use hasing to be sure websocket connection and entries in redis.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
